    ip6n->fb_tnl_dev->rtnl_link_ops = &vti6_link_ops;
    // missing: ip6n->fb_tnl_dev->netns_immutable = true;
Reason:
The fallback device ip6_vti0 was created in vti6_init_net() without setting the netns_immutable flag. This omission allows the device to be moved to another network namespace, which is inconsistent with other similar tunnel drivers (e.g., ip6_tunnel, sit) and can lead to security or stability issues.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
